------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running BusTalk simulations. 

Ensure that the following variables are set as per the user's
local environment settings.

eg : setenv GLOBAL /h/arm/global 

eg : setenv DIRS_VERILOG /NIS/backup/ARMOURY/armdata/AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/verilog/cb25os163/zero

eg : setenv FILES_VERILOG /NIS/backup/ARMOURY/armdata/AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/verilog/cb25os163/zero/mtb_verilog.v

eg : setenv LIB_SYNOP /NIS/backup/ARMOURY/armdata/AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/synopsys/cb25os163/1997.01/models

Please note that the above paths are EXAMPLE paths.

setenv PERIPH Periph

Additionally set the following environment variables to control
simulations using a modelsim simulator. 

Rtl Simulations
---------------
setenv SIMULATOR modelsim
setenv HDL_SOURCE verilog

Netlist Simulations
-------------------
setenv SIMULATOR modelsim
setenv TEST_METH noscan
setenv HDL_SOURCE vhdl
setenv HDL_NETL verilog

Set the following environment variables to control simulations using a 
LDV simulator. 

setenv SIMULATOR LDV
setenv TEST_METH scanready
setenv HDL_SOURCE verilog
setenv HDL_NETL verilog

1. VERILOG RTL simulations (For both modelsim and LDV simulations)
------------------------------------------------------------------
- In the verification/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to verification/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create verification/bustest/invec/bif.sim

- In the verification/verilog/ directory
  'make rtl'

2. VERILOG NETLIST simulations (For modelsim simulator)
------------------------------------------------------
- In the verification/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to verification/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create verification/bustest/invec/bif.sim

- In the verification/verilog/ directory
  'make net_min'

  This will perform a MINIMUM timing annotated simulation 
  on the VERILOG netlist generated from VHDL RTL. 

3. VERILOG SCAN NETLIST simulations (For LDV simulator)
------------------------------------------------------
- In the verification/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to verification/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create verification/bustest/invec/bif.sim

- In the verification/verilog/ directory
  'make net_typ'

  This will perform a TYPICAL timing annotated simulation 
  on the scanready VERILOG netlist generated from VERILOG
  RTL. 

